{
  "analysis": "I can see the thresholds file and partial SKILL.md content. The output was truncated. I need to see the full SKILL.md to understand the complete requirements for the composite risk light calculation and output format.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file to get all the requirements, then create the output.json with the signal board, composite risk light, actionable notes, and data gaps.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -100\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have all the information needed. The thresholds file shows 10 indicators with their thresholds and tiers. The SKILL.md explains the output format: Signal Board, Composite Risk Light (GREEN/YELLOW/ORANGE/RED), Actionable Notes, and Data Gaps. The composite rule is: YELLOW if Tier A >= 2 triggered, ORANGE if Tier A >= 2 AND Tier B >= 1, RED if all three tiers have triggers. Let me analyze: Tier A: A2(0.72>0.7), A3(0.24>0.2), A4(0.63>0.6) = 3 triggered. Tier B: B2(96>90), B3(17>15) = 2 triggered. Tier C: C1(0.031>0.03), C2(-0.008>-0.01), C3(0.017>0.015) = 3 triggered. This gives RED status.",
  "plan": "Create output.json with the required structure: signal_board (10 indicators with value, trend, threshold_status), composite_risk_light (RED), actionable_notes, and data_gaps (identifying stale inputs like A3 and C2 from March).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > output.json << 'EOF'
{
  "report_date": "2025-05-01",
  "signal_board": [
    {"id": "A1", "name": "Job postings for AI-exposed roles", "value": 0.81, "unit": "index", "trend": "down", "threshold": 0.85, "status": "normal"},
    {"id": "A2", "name": "Resume response rate for displaced workers", "value": 0.72, "unit": "rate", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.7, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "A3", "name": "AI capex growth", "value": 0.24, "unit": "yoy", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.2, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "A4", "name": "AI labor substitution speed", "value": 0.63, "unit": "index", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.6, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "B1", "name": "Unemployment rate in affected occupations", "value": 0.058, "unit": "rate", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.06, "status": "normal"},
    {"id": "B2", "name": "Median re-employment duration", "value": 96, "unit": "days", "trend": "up", "threshold": 90, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "B3", "name": "Layoff announcements in exposed sectors", "value": 17, "unit": "count", "trend": "up", "threshold": 15, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "C1", "name": "Consumer delinquency rate", "value": 0.031, "unit": "rate", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.03, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "C2", "name": "Retail spending growth", "value": -0.008, "unit": "yoy", "trend": "down", "threshold": -0.01, "status": "triggered"},
    {"id": "C3", "name": "Credit spread widening", "value": 0.017, "unit": "spread", "trend": "up", "threshold": 0.015, "status": "triggered"}
  ],
  "composite_risk_light": "RED",
  "tier_summary": {
    "tier_a_triggers": 3,
    "tier_b_triggers": 2,
    "tier_c_triggers": 3
  },
  "actionable_notes": [
    "Elevated risk posture warranted: AI substitution accelerating across all tiers",
    "Tier A shows strong displacement signals (A2, A3, A4 triggered) despite A1 easing",
    "Labor market confirmation present: re-employment duration and layoffs both elevated",
    "Macro spillover emerging: consumer delinquency, spending slowdown, credit stress all triggered",
    "Monitor capex absorption: high AI investment may eventually create re-absorption opportunities",
    "Consider defensive positioning in credit-sensitive sectors until displacement signals normalize"
  ],
  "data_gaps": [
    {"indicator": "A3", "issue": "stale", "details": "Quarterly data from 2025-03-31 is over 30 days old"},
    {"indicator": "C2", "issue": "stale", "details": "Monthly data from 2025-03-31 is over 30 days old"}
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The output.json file has been created with 2501 bytes. The content shows all 10 indicators in the signal_board, composite_risk_light set to RED (correct based on the rules: Tier A has 3 triggers, Tier B has 2, Tier C has 3), actionable notes, and data gaps. I should verify the JSON is valid and machine-readable.",
  "plan": "Verify the JSON is valid by parsing it with Python's json module, then confirm the task is complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import json; data=json.load(open('output.json')); print('Valid JSON'); print('Signal board:', len(data['signal_board'])); print('Risk light:', data['composite_risk_light']); print('Notes:', len(data['actionable_notes'])); print('Data gaps:', len(data['data_gaps']))\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The output.json file has been successfully created and validated. It contains:\n- 10 indicators in the signal_board with value, trend, threshold, and status\n- composite_risk_light set to RED (correct: Tier A has 3 triggers, Tier B has 2, Tier C has 3 - meeting all RED criteria)\n- 6 actionable notes with portfolio/risk posture suggestions\n- 2 data gaps identifying stale inputs (A3 and C2 from March 2025)\n\nThe JSON is valid and machine-readable as verified by Python's json module.",
